From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:01:58 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 290/297] Meridian: Settings > AI > Agents can use: all spaces
 or only some

"All spaces" (the default) or "Only these", with a switch per space
("Only these" starts with the space on screen). Agents don't see the
others: list_spaces, list_tabs and search_tabs leave them out (favorites,
in every space, stay), and a tool given one of their tabs or pinned items,
or working on the current tab there, is refused with a message naming the
space and the setting. open_tab into a refused space fails; with no space
named it opens in one agents may use. Prefs meridian.agent_spaces and
meridian.agent_space_ids on the main profile; Settings fields appended.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
